{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only models dominate (best: scvi_n200 + multiprofile at ~0.65 acc), while image-only models are weak (best: resnet50 + multiprofile at ~0.33 acc). The critical open question is whether the image modality, despite its weak standalone performance, provides complementary information (e.g., morphology) that improves predictions when fused with the strong RNA signal. This experiment (config_030: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) directly tests that question by adding image to the best-known RNA configuration (config_005, acc 0.650) while keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation identical. Using concat (simpler than weighted) and resnet50 (already characterized) keeps the comparison clean. If accuracy improves meaningfully over 0.650, image adds value and we should explore the multimodal space; if it does not, we can eliminate the majority of remaining multimodal configs and focus on refining the RNA-only pipeline. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design decision (unimodal vs. multimodal) under the limited budget."
}

